      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moenkopi%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town splits into Upper Moenkopi, the more traditional community, and Lower Moenkopi, the younger community pursuing modern pursuits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://ehillerman.unm.edu/1970-0"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Moenkopi occupies a 250‑square‑mile exclave of the Hopi Reservation, surrounded on all sides by Navajo Nation land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moenkopi%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Moenkopi Day School, a Bureau of Indian Education tribal school, serves the community’s children.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
